    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0141" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760 D.61/655: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Panamanian Minister for
                        Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-12">December 12,
                        1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I desire to acknowledge receipt of Your Excellency’s telegram of December 6,
                    1939, in which reference is made to Section 4 of Resolution 10 adopted at the
                    meeting of the Foreign Ministers of the American Republics regarding “the
                    invasion of weak nations as an expedient for the prosecution and winning of
                    wars” and in which you undertake to rouse all the American Republics to protest
                    against the invasion and occupation of Finland.</p>
                <p>Consonant with the spirit which motivated President Roosevelt in the issuance of
                    his statement of December 1 condemning the Soviet resort to military force
                    against Finland, this Government is prepared to associate itself with the
                    governments of the other American republics in a joint statement of vigorous
                    protest against the invasion of Finland.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
